# Where the sessions go

Two hops, acyclic, and every node conserves what flows through it. The columns
are a longest path and `align: justify` anchors both ends, which is what puts
the three exits in one column instead of scattering them by depth.

```mdv sankey
title: Sessions by source and outcome
source: from
target: to
value: sessions
nodeWidth: 12
nodePadding: 8
align: justify
format: table
---
from      | to        | sessions
Organic   | Product   |    18240
Organic   | Docs      |     8110
Direct    | Product   |    12470
Direct    | Docs      |     3060
Referral  | Product   |     4980
Referral  | Docs      |     2210
Paid      | Product   |     6320
Paid      | Docs      |     1140
Product   | Signed up |    21880
Product   | Bounced   |    20130
Docs      | Signed up |     3410
Docs      | Bounced   |    11120
```
